# Linker version script for AIFX .ofx plugins (GNU ld / Linux).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS — symbol interposition crash on Flame/Linux.
#
# AIFX links every dependency statically into each .ofx (zlib via miniz/tinyexr,
# OpenSSL, httplib, ixwebsocket, the OFX C++ Support library, ...). Those archives
# are compiled with *default* ELF visibility, so without this script the .ofx
# re-exports ~3700 of their symbols (crc32, adler32, deflate/inflate, EXRLayers,
# the whole OpenSSL surface, ...).
#
# A host like Flame is a huge binary that links its OWN copies of zlib/OpenSSL/
# OpenEXR. When it dlopen()s the plugin, ELF's global symbol table lets the host's
# internal calls bind to the PLUGIN's crc32/deflate/etc. (interposition). The host
# then runs its image/codec/IO paths against a different zlib/OpenSSL build than it
# was compiled for and segfaults (observed: SIGSEGV at 0x0 the instant the effect
# is instantiated, Flame/Linux only — macOS dyld uses a two-level namespace and is
# immune, which is why Resolve/macOS never hit this).
#
# Fix: an OFX plugin's ABI is exactly three C entry points. Export only those and
# localize everything else, so no dependency symbol can leak out and interpose the
# host (or be interposed by it).
{
    global:
        OfxGetNumberOfPlugins;
        OfxGetPlugin;
        OfxSetHost;   # OFX 1.4+ optional entry point; harmless if undefined
    local:
        *;
};
